From: FastDDS standards A1 work
Subject: [PATCH] 3.6.2 EDP: opt into bounded TypeObject assignability

Applies to pristine v3.6.2. A1.0 architecture exception explicitly approved
by the project owner on 2026-11-11. No Transport-specific behaviour.
Reference: https://www.omg.org/spec/DDS-XTypes/1.3/PDF
Sections 7.2.4.4.8 and 7.6.3.4.2.

FASTDDS_XTYPES_HONOR_TYPE_CONSISTENCY must equal exactly "1". The gate is
process-wide, read once; unset/other values retain stock decisions. Gate ON
honours each reader's type consistency policy: equivalent types retain the
stock fast path; non-equivalent types require ALLOW_TYPE_COERCION and
registered TypeObjects. Forced validation rejects missing TypeInformation.

A1 subset: non-inherited final/appendable/mutable structs, at most 256 members
in each non-equivalent definition; member correspondence by ID and optionally
name (or name hash); equal extensibility; appendable/final ordering; final
member-set equality; required/key members; prevent_type_widening for non-optional writer-only
members. Corresponding optional/key flags must agree (a conservative subset,
including mutable structs). Matched
member types must be equivalent or same-encoding-width string identifiers
whose bounds satisfy reader policy (key string bounds always checked).
Other non-equivalent member types, inheritance and constructs fail closed.
This is NOT a complete XTypes assignability implementation. Numeric coercion,
alias expansion, recursive type evolution, unions and differing collection
bounds are not claimed. TypeLookup and all other matching/QoS paths are
unchanged. No asynchronous requests, registry lock retention or new resources.

